@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+Feature: Routing
+  As a user
+  I want to filter the todo list by completion state
+  So that I can focus on active or completed tasks
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+    And the todo list has items "Buy milk", "Walk dog", "Write code"
+    And the user completes "Buy milk"
+
+  Rule: Default route shows all todos
+
+  Scenario: Default route shows all todos
+    Given the current route is "#/"
+    Then the todo list shows 3 items
+    And the "All" filter link has the selected class
+
+  Rule: Active filter
+
+  Scenario: Active filter shows only active todos
+    When the user clicks the "Active" filter link
+    Then the todo list shows 2 items
+    And those items are "Walk dog" and "Write code"
+    And the "Active" filter link has the selected class
+
+  Rule: Completed filter
+
+  Scenario: Completed filter shows only completed todos
+    When the user clicks the "Completed" filter link
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item
+    And that item is "Buy milk"
+    And the "Completed" filter link has the selected class
+
+  Rule: Filtered state after update
+
+  Scenario: Completing a todo hides it in the active filter
+    Given the active filter is selected
+    When the user completes "Walk dog"
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item
+    And that item is "Write code"
+
+  Scenario: Un-completing a todo shows it in the completed filter
+    Given the completed filter is selected
+    When the user toggles "Buy milk" back to active
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Rule: Route persistence
+
+  Scenario: Active filter persists across reload
+    Given the active filter is selected
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the "Active" filter link has the selected class
+    And the todo list shows only active items
